From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francisco Huelsz Prince <frhuelsz@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] container: Allow privileged containers to dbus kernel_t

On ACL, /usr ships with no SELinux labels, so dbus-daemon and other host
services currently run as kernel_t instead of their intended labeled
domains (init_t, system_dbusd_t, systemd_machined_t). Until that is
fixed, a privileged container's first D-Bus message to the system bus
is denied, because the policy only permits privileged_container_domain
to talk to the labeled domains, not to kernel_t.

Tested: adding this rule alone (without any relabeling) resolves the
denial, with no further denials observed.

Signed-off-by: Francisco Huelsz Prince <frhuelsz@microsoft.com>
---
 policy/modules/services/container.te | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/policy/modules/services/container.te b/policy/modules/services/container.te
--- a/policy/modules/services/container.te
+++ b/policy/modules/services/container.te
@@ -1025,6 +1025,12 @@
 	systemd_dbus_chat_logind(privileged_container_domain)
 ')
 
+# ACL: /usr ships unlabeled, so dbus-daemon and other host services currently
+# run as kernel_t rather than their intended labeled domains. Until that is
+# fixed, a privileged container is denied its first D-Bus message to the
+# system bus.
+allow spc_t kernel_t:dbus send_msg;
+
 ########################################
 #
 # spc local policy
-- 
